Patch PHP's Windows build to work with conda-forge library names.

conda-forge provides different .lib filenames than what the PHP SDK expects,
so the CHECK_LIB search lists below are widened accordingly.

php_iconv.def additionally drops the GNU libiconv symbols. conda-forge's
iconv.lib has no _libiconv_version, and because that is a *data* symbol it
cannot be re-exported from php8ts.dll the way the four libiconv* functions
can, so leaving it in the .def fails the link with:

    php8ts.dll.def : error LNK2001: unresolved external symbol _libiconv_version

The replacement comment line in that hunk is load-bearing, not decoration:
rattler-build >= 0.70 (flickzeug) silently drops a hunk that consists only of
context and deletion lines when it has leading but no trailing context, which
is exactly the shape of a pure "delete the last 5 lines" hunk. Keeping one
inserted line in the hunk sidesteps that bug. Once it is fixed upstream the
comment can go away.

This patch is machine-generated (git diff); regenerate it rather than editing
hunk headers by hand.

diff --git a/ext/curl/config.w32 b/ext/curl/config.w32
index 4f8e3448..370c1587 100644
